silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_15_cocone_apex_and_naturality_sections_01_cocone_apex_construction_step_by_step_concrete_anchor_24_CocLegCompatibility#coclegcompatibility a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.15_cocone_apex_and_naturality.sections.01_cocone_apex_construction_step_by_step.concrete_anchor_24_CocLegCompatibility#coclegcompatibility" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_15_cocone_apex_and_naturality_sections_01_cocone_apex_construction_step_by_step_concrete_anchor_24_CocLegCompatibility#coclegcompatibility silm:hasLongDescription "The CocLegCompatibility is the universal cocone-leg compatibility law: all incoming legs agree on the apex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CocLegCompatibility', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
